spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.0384050231112939,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":24.6,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.028301420943447085,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":42.6,"_gate_share_shrink":0.010001424580791562,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":37.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.47950589556428974,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.16381,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"FVCBankcorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for FVCbank provides various banking products and services for small and medium-sized businesses, professionals, non-profit organizations and associations, and investors. The company provides various deposit products which includes interest and noninterest-bearing transaction accounts, certificates of deposit, savings, and money market accounts. It offers lending products comprising commercial real estate loans; commercial construction loans; commercial loans for a range of business purposes, such as for working capital, equipment purchases, lines of credit, and government contract financing; small business administration lending; asset based lending and accounts receivable financing; home equity loans or home equity lines of credit; and consumer loans for constructive purposes. In addition, the company provides business and consumer credit cards; merchant services; business insurance products; and digital banking, remote deposit, and mobile banking services. FVCBankcorp, Inc. was founded in 2007 and is headquartered in Fairfax, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. David W. Pijor Esq. | Founder, CEO & Chairman | Age 73 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 134 people. Revenue per employee of $13K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue falling 36%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $178K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 116\u00d7 revenue per employee (high relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["FVCBankcorp, Inc. is a micro-cap financial services business with a $293M market cap on $2M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -70% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +222.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $24M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 1337 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.08\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 48% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 61.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 55/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 1557% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 58% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Contrast: Fvcbankcorp (NASDAQ:FVCB) vs. Banner (NASDAQ:BANR)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/critical-contrast-fvcbankcorp-nasdaqfvcb-vs-banner-nasdaqbanr.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794518115.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.82,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(FVCB) Risk Channels and Responsive Allocation","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/FVCB_Risk_Channels_and_Responsive_Allocation_111126111002_1794413402.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794413402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.202,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(FVCB) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/17/FVCB_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110126111202_1793549522.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793549522.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"FVCBankcorp, Inc. (NASDAQ:FVCB) Looks Interesting, And It's About To Pay A Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-fvcb/fvcbankcorp/news/fvcbankcorp-inc-nasdaqfvcb-looks-interesting-and-its-about-t","date":"2026-10-23","timestamp":1792762827.51,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"FVCBankcorp (FVCB) Lags Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3013338/fvcbankcorp-fvcb-lags-q3-earnings-and-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3013338","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792702805.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.361,"t